  "summary": "Malicious code in quillonatts (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (fad09c871f903768f458b780fd73be2cea587a7217ace4c10fa46941883e905d)\nThe package quillonatts 0.1.0 does not exhibit traced behavior consistent with supply-chain attack shapes. No install-time or import-time outbound network activity, no credential or environment-variable harvesting, no shell execution of fetched content, no persistence mechanism, and no silent-relay or backdoor code paths were observed in the shipped files.\n\n## Source: kam193 (6297f0fae1c96dd5abefc4dd7f67a51ee7a737d1bb437fcffaed067d44d637a4)\nThis campaign consists of similar loader packages, which provide executing code from a given URL. While they do not contain the malicious payload and the usage remains unknown, they are clearly a coordinated campaign to place multiple deceptive ways to load malicious code.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-voice-synthesis-profiles\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - other\n",
